1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In this tutorial video, we use the 11th version of DOS Marvelous Designer.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
If you need to learn the 10th version of Marvelous Designer, please watch the quick introduction video released before.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
In order to make it easier to learn, DOS is used in this tutorial.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
When using Marvelous Designer, you can draw the board in 2D or 3D windows.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
In this tutorial video, you will learn how to make a T-shirt mountain in 3D windows.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000
By drawing the board in 3D windows, you can determine the basic shape of the board,

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
which helps you to learn the course of drawing boards in 2D windows.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Drawing boards in 3D windows directly helps you to create basic costumes quickly for your unique virtual model.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
First, we need to introduce a virtual model.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Here we have a virtual model.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
We will open the Vimeo VR file folder.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Select the 3D model tool and select the virtual model tool in the drop-down menu.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Click on the middle point in the foreground to create a starting point.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Then move the mouse to draw the front and middle lines.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Press the Shift key to draw a line along the horizontal or vertical direction.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Press the left mouse button in the right position.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Continue to press the Shift key to move the mouse to preview the line.

18
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Press the left mouse button in the left position of the horizontal line.

19
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Continue to move the mouse to draw the side line.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Since the model's waist line is a curve, we need to create a curve on the horizontal line.

21
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Press the left mouse button in the right position to create a curve.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
This is the curve.

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Release the Ctrl key and press the left mouse button in the lower position to create a straight line.

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Complete the drawing of the horizontal line.

25
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Next, we will draw a curve along the sleeve.

26
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Remember to press the Ctrl key to create a curve.

27
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Release the Ctrl key and press the right mouse button in the left position to create a straight line.

28
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
After the curve is created, press the Shift key and click on the mouse button to create a shoulder line.

29
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Continue to draw a curve and then click on the starting point to complete the drawing of the template.

30
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Before we remove the template from the 2D window, we need to set the front, middle, bottom, and shoulder lines as straight lines.

31
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Change the tool to Edit Line Virtual Model.

32
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Right-click on these 3D lines and select Edit Line as Straight Line.

33
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:42,000
The line that is edited as a straight line will be displayed as a thicker line.

34
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Select the mouse and select the Edit Line tool in the drop-down menu.

35
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Select the mouse in the created template area.

36
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Move the mouse to click on the mouse when the area changes to blue.

37
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
After selecting, the area changes to yellow. Press the Enter key to extract the template.

38
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Now the front will be extracted to the 2D window.

39
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Now we create the back of the template in the same way.

40
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,000
I will start drawing from the highest point of the shoulder, then draw the back, middle, waist, and shoulder line.

41
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
First, draw the back.

42
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Press the Shift key and click on the mouse button to draw the back, middle, and then complete the bottom line along the vertical direction.

43
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Click on the side point created before and complete the bottom creation.

44
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Since the side line has been drawn, I am now going to draw the shoulder line.

45
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Start from the bottom point that has been drawn.

46
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Draw a curve along the virtual model body curve.

47
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Click on the side point to complete the creation.

48
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Same as the front, set the back, middle, and bottom lines as a straight line.

49
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Next is the sleeve version.

50
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Start from the side point on the outside.

51
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Draw a straight line as the sleeve middle line according to your needs.

52
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Press the Ctrl key along the arm circle to draw the sleeve bottom line.

53
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Continue to draw the inside edge of the sleeve until it is connected to the bottom point.

54
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Repeat the operation to complete the other half of the sleeve version.

55
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:15,000
After completion, select the Edit line virtual model tool.

56
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Set the sleeve middle line to a flat straight line.

57
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Then select the flat as a version tool.

58
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Click on two areas of the sleeve version to remove it as a version.

59
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Now the sleeve version on one side is completed.

60
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Now the sleeve version on one side is completed.

61
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,000
We need to adjust some lines more smoothly.

62
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Select the Edit version of the sleeve tool and press the E key.

63
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Press the Shift key to click on the two straight lines in the center of the front.

64
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
At the same time, click on the right button at the bottom to select the right axis.

65
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
The front will become a vertical line.

66
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
In the same way, select the two straight lines at the bottom.

67
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
In the right-hand menu, select the right axis.

68
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The lower line of the X-axis will become a horizontal line in the 2D window.

69
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Adjust the back piece in the same way.

70
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
In the right-hand menu, select the right axis.

71
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
In the left-hand menu, select the right axis.

72
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
For the sleeve version, we need to rotate them first to the right position, then the parallel version.

73
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Change to the adjustment version tool.

74
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Right-click on the sleeve version and select Rotate.

75
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,000
The mouse is located on a line.

76
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
You can see that the rotation of this line and the rotation of the y-axis are parallel.

77
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Click on the release effect of the version to complete the rotation.

78
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Now let's modify the inner line of the sleeve and the bottom.

79
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
On the edit version tool, select the mouse.

80
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
You can find the edit curve point and the edit element tool in the drop-down menu.

81
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Select the edit curve point tool or press the V key,

82
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
then select the inner line once, the curve point on the bottom,

83
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
and delete them with the Delete key.

84
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Select the edit version tool or press the Z key.

85
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Repeat the previous operation to remove the inner line and the bottom of the sleeve.

86
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Now we will learn how to merge two versions into one version.

87
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Select the middle line of the two versions,

88
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
then right-click on the selected line and select Merge.

89
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Please note that after merging, the original line will no longer exist.

90
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Now let's adjust the sleeve curve and the sleeve mountain curve of the mountain.

91
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Select the edit curve point and press the V key,

92
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
select the edit curve point tool,

93
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
refer to the video, delete the useless curve point,

94
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
and keep the sleeve curve line as an O curve.

95
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Then use the edit original curve tool,

96
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
refer to the version in the video, drag the sleeve curve line to the appropriate curve.

97
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Use the same method to adjust the sleeve mountain curve line.

98
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:56,000
In this way, one side of the sleeve curve is moreบ,

99
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:18,000
and one side is less 0.

100
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
On the right-hand side of the version that has been adjusted, select and .

101
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:29,000
After using this function, the version created will be synchronized with the original version.

102
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
The line will be symmetrical.

103
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Please place the version in the 2D window.

104
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Use the same method to create a symmetrical version of the sleeve and the back.

105
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Next is the pocket version of the chest.

106
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Select the 3D version tool in the 3D tool bar.

107
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Draw a rectangular pocket line according to the need.

108
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Then switch to the 3D version tool in the edit point line in the download menu.

109
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Select all the lines that form the pocket.

110
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Click and select the inner shape of the collage.

111
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
The pocket line will be created on two front pieces at the same time.

112
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Because they are in a symmetrical relationship, select the edit curve tool to delete the excess curve points.

113
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Adjust the pocket to a symmetrical rectangular shape.

114
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:16,000
We will later extract the pocket version of the sewing box based on this rectangular shape.

115
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
The mouse is attached to the edit version tool group.

116
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
In the download menu, select the collage outline tool.

117
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Select the rectangular shape in the box and click the selected pattern on the right.

118
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Select the collage as a version.

119
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Select the collage as a version.

120
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Select the collage as a version.

121
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Please note that the collage as a version does not have a link function.

122
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
What is extracted is an independent version.

123
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Now we have completed the creation of a set of T-shirt versions.

124
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Please save this project as a project file.

125
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:53,000
We will use this project file in the future teaching video.

